{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH will reign forever and ever.</b> May it be His will that He reign over us forever and ever — such a Master who did these good things for us. Another interpretation: it is in the language of present and future, as in its Targum. Like כנשר יעיר קנו, ירחף, יפרוש כנפיו, יקחהו, ישאהו — and many more." "<b>לעלם ועד.</b> It is a shortened form, which is like לעולם ועד לעולם. And do not wonder about the word עולם ועד that it is not in construct state, for we find a parallel: שוכן עד וקדוש שמו, whose meaning is 'who dwells forever on high, and holy is His name.' And the rule of the holy language is that when the vowel is under the letter after the vav, it is opened with a patach — like שור, וכשב, ועז; therefore ועד is opened. And we find ואוכל at the end of the verse, and at the end of the verse הנחש השיאני ואוכל — therefore it is לעולם ועד."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The final sentence appears to argue from parallel cases of words at verse-ends; the logic and the citation of 'the end of the verse' twice is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:05.084401470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}